      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "bca283ee-7bdc-58ce-880d-80fd4fc26441",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James MacGregor, George V, Queen Victoria, Edward VII\n- Roles: Moderator of the General Assembly of the Church of Scotland, Chaplain in Ordinary, Chaplain\n- Organizations: Church of Scotland\n- Topics: Scottish ministry, philanthropy, British monarchy\n\nFacts:\n- James MacGregor was a Scottish minister and philanthropist who lived from 1832 to 1910.\n- George V, born George Frederick Ernest Albert, was born on 3 June 1865.\n- In 1886, James MacGregor was made Chaplain in Ordinary to Queen Victoria.\n- In 1891, James MacGregor served as Moderator of the General Assembly of the Church of Scotland.\n- In 1901, James MacGregor became Chaplain to King Edward VII.\n- On 6 May 1910, George V became King of the United Kingdom and the British Dominions and Emperor of India.\n- In 1910, James MacGregor became Chaplain to King George V, serving three monarchs in all.\n- James MacGregor died in 1910.\n- George V remained king until his death on 20 January 1936.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
